-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart with level, branch and inertia riders
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((t))$ (the field of Laurent series over $L$), required by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is: the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\big)$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A\to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L\subseteq K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=t^{-1}\cdot jNumQ$, the classical $j$-expansion over $\mathbb Q$, and let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   Let $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model: the pushout in schemes of the two maps out of the middle chart into $X_{\mathrm{fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ and $X_{\infty}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and let $\varpi z$ be, as `hϖz` prescribes, the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained by pulling back $\varpi$ along `toBase`; the hypothesis `hz` asks that $\varpi z$ lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$. Let $y$ be a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ mapped to $z$ by the chart immersion `ιFin`. The supersingularity hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` (the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$) to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain, a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and
--   $$f-\big(X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1\big)\in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v-f\,u\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ is the adic completion of the stalk at its maximal ideal, such that the following four assertions hold. Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the canonical map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map $W[[X_0,X_1]]\to S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical ring homomorphism from the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` to the stalk at $z$, obtained from the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ adjunction isomorphism, the isomorphism on sections of the chart immersion `ιFin` over the top open, and the germ map at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin`.
--
--   (1) Compatibility with the base: for every $a\in A$, $e$ carries the image in $\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ of the germ at $z$ of the pullback of $a$ along `toBase` to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$.
--
--   (2) Level automorphisms and their linear parts: for every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e.: for every weight $k\in\mathbb Z$, all modular forms $F,G$ of weight $k$ for the subgroup of $GL_2(\mathbb R)$ attached to $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with $H$ as above, all integral power series $p_F,p_G$ whose images in $\mathbb C[[t]]$ are the $q$-expansions (width $1$) of $F,G$, with the Laurent series of $p_G$ over $\mathbb Q$ nonzero, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_F/p_G$, and every ring embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, one has
--   $$\iota_*\big((\tau x)\big)\cdot q\text{-exp}\big(G\mid_k c(\gamma^{-1})\big)=q\text{-exp}\big(F\mid_k c(\gamma^{-1})\big),$$
--   where for $\gamma^{-1}=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\ c&d\end{pmatrix}$ the matrix $c(\gamma^{-1})$ is $\begin{pmatrix}a& b/(q\ell)\\ (q\ell)c& d\end{pmatrix}$ — the following holds: for every proof that $\tau$ maps the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` into itself, if the induced endomorphism of the chart algebra satisfies $\tau(a)-a\in y$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra, then there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta\circ e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}=e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}\circ\tau$ on the chart algebra; $\theta$ fixes every constant class $\mathrm{mkS}(C w)$, $w\in W$; for each index $jj$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{jj}))-\mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_{ii}C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$; $c^{q+1}-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; $M_{ii\,jj}-c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj}\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $ii,jj$ (entries of $\gamma$ cast from $\mathbb Z$ to $W$); if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   (3) Identification of the anchored branch with the Gauss valuation: for every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ such that at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$ is not in $P$, such that $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))\in P$, and such that there is $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $\mathrm{mkS}\big(C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h\big)\in P$, one has for every $a$ in the chart algebra: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the preimage of $P$ under $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $L((t))$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under $A\to L$, i.e. for each $n\in\mathbb Z$ there is $m\in\mathfrak m_A$ with $\mathrm{coeff}_n(a)=$ the image of $m$.
--
--   (4) Tame inertia: for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, every ring automorphism $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and every ring automorphism $\sigma_A$ of $A$ such that $\sigma_A$ is compatible with $\sigma_L$ under $A\to L$, such that $\sigma_A(a)-a\in\mathfrak m_A$ for all $a\in A$, and such that $\sigma_L(\zeta)=\zeta^{\,\mathrm{val}(d)}$, and for every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting on Laurent series coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$, the following hold: $\tau$ maps the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` into itself; and for every proof of this preservation, the induced endomorphism satisfies $\tau(a)-a\in y$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra, and there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta\circ e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}=e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}\circ\tau$ on the chart algebra; $\sigma_W\circ\sigma=\sigma\circ\sigma_A$ on $A$; $\sigma_W(w)-w\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $w\in W$; $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(Cw))=\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_W w))$ for all $w\in W$, so that $\theta$ is $\sigma_W$-semilinear on constants; for each $jj$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{jj}))-\mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_{ii}C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; and for all $ii,jj$, $M_{ii\,jj}$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_W$ to the image in $W$ of the entry $\big(d\cdot\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^{q})^{-1})\big)_{ii\,jj}$ of the scalar multiple by $d$ of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.diagOneElem q (d^q)⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L233) over $\mathbb Z/q$ (each entry taken via its representative in $\{0,\dots,q-1\}$); since $d^{q}=d$ in $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, this matrix is $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$.
--
--   This is the local-structure statement at a supersingular point of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$: the completed local ring is presented as a Drinfeld-type crossing $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varpi v-fu)$ with $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ to order $q+2$, together with the linear parts of the level automorphisms, the identification of the branch anchored in the direction $(1,0)$ with the Gauss valuation on $q$-expansions, and the linear part $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$ of tame inertia. It packages the core chart theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel) with the inertia clause supplied by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_diagOneElem_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_diagOneElem_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel), and is used in the subsequent passage to an algebraically closed residue situation in the analysis of the $q$-adic reduction of the relevant Jacobians.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_inertia_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel.lean

